Backstage Forever normalization: each build's creatures.json is normalized
separately, then merged newest-first into 3272 creature identities: name
(newest named build wins; 8 rows were never named and stay null), the
observed level range (lowest and highest level seen in any build; level -1,
shown in game as "??", is kept as a skull flag), elite (elite or rare elite),
rare (rare or rare elite) and world boss flags (set if any build saw them),
hostileTo and the contributing-file count (largest single-build count).
hostileTo lists the factions (Alliance, Horde) for which any observation
recorded a UnitReaction of 3 (unfriendly) or lower; 4 is neutral and 5 or
more friendly. Rows seen only in combat logs (no classification or reaction),
positions, world coordinates, experience, reputation, deaths, combat log
details and personal records are excluded. Raw file sizes/hashes/metadata and
compiled size/hash are pinned in source-lock.json. No runtime network request
is needed.

These are approximate historical community observations, not guaranteed
levels, spawns, difficulty or complete coverage. A creature that no player of
a faction met may still be hostile to that faction. Contributing saved files
are not distinct witnesses or confidence ratings. The license does not grant
rights in Blizzard narrative text or game assets.
